    "body": "Just my two cents:\r\n\r\nhttps://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#biblio-mimetype cites \r\n\r\n>[Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) Part Two: Media Types](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2046). November 1996. Draft Standard. URL: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2046\r\n\r\nThe authoritative source names itself \"Media Types\" and describes media types.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, there are [Media Type Specifications and Registration Procedures](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6838.html), [Media Types](https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml) etc.\r\n\r\nAFAICT, that use of the term \"media type\" predates other uses.\r\n\r\nWouldn't it be more appropriate to refer to the name as intended?\r\n",
